,"    \/\/ ...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To instantiate this layout using the default center alignment, you don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have to specify the alignment value, but you do need to add empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parentheses:"}]},{"syntax":null,"code":["BasicVStack() {","    \/\/ ...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift compiler requires the parentheses in this case because of how the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout protocol implements this call site syntax. Specifically, the layout’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/callAsFunction(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method looks for an initializer with exactly zero"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input arguments when you omit the parentheses from the call site."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can enable the simpler call site for a layout that doesn’t have an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implicit initializer of this type by explicitly defining one:"}]},{"syntax":null,"code":["init() {","    self.alignment = .center","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For information about Swift initializers, see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Initialization.html","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift Programming Language"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Interact with subviews through their proxies","level":3,"anchor":"Interact-with-subviews-through-their-proxies","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To perform layout, you need information about all of its subviews, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are the views that your container arranges. While your layout can’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interact directly with its subviews, it can access a set of subview proxies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/Subviews","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" collection that each protocol method receives as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an input parameter. That type is an alias for the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubviews","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection type, which in turn contains "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" instances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that are the subview proxies."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can get information about each subview from its proxy, like its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dimensions and spacing preferences. This enables","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you to measure subviews before you commit to placing them. You also","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assign a position to each subview by calling its proxy’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/place(at:anchor:proposal:)","isActive":true},{"text":" method.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Call the method on each subview from within your implementation of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layo